      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18869",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/08/0855f54843f5fda20a37868b5266da6d3ec41aa641b25ce38bf4c6cfcd09b56d.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curves $x =-y + \\frac{y^{3}}{2}$ and $x =-\\frac{y^{3}}{2}$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are quarter-circles, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
