      ":question/problem": "![](images/fd/fdf509bcb9b77fa8ef71185968b6be321f3ec1beb8643182045b9508e7132eae.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $x = y - y^{2}$ and the line $x =-y$, as shown in the picture. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are semicircles, which of the following gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
